.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt RESOLVD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm resolvd
.Nd RavenBSD DNS resolver service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads IPv4 nameservers from
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
and registers the
.Dq resolv:
scheme.  A client opens the control file and sends one
.Sy CALL
with a query; the reply carries A/AAAA records, NXDOMAIN, or an error.
Each query uses a bounded UDP exchange through
.Xr netd 8 :
one retry per configured server, a 500 ms per-attempt timeout, and CNAME
following bounded to eight links.  The service never invents an address and
does not cache across queries.
.Pp
Only the
.Sy nameserver
directive is interpreted; IPv4 addresses are used.  A static
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
wins.  DHCP lease application is not wired in this milestone: it needs the
netd/B12b/B12c interface for a real link and lease state.
.Sh PROTOCOL
The control file is
.Pa resolv: .
A query is little-endian: version 1 (u16), query type (u8; 1 = A, 28 = AAAA),
name length (u16), and the ASCII name.  A reply is version 1, status (0 =
answers, 1 = NXDOMAIN, 2 = error), query type, record count, then records of
type (u8), TTL (u32), and 4 or 16 address bytes.  At most eight records fit.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
Static nameserver list.
.It Pa /etc/services.d/resolvd.toml
Service manifest.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
A malformed query or reply returns
.Er EINVAL
or
.Er EPROTO .
A nonexistent name returns the NXDOMAIN reply.
A timeout or transport failure is reported as an error reply, not an empty
answer.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr netd 8 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
RFC 1035 and RFC 2131 are the DNS and DHCP references.
